From c6bfeeb7f3410014851e9460493c8ddb112c92b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:50:15 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] mptcp: extend kcov coverage to the non-DSS option
 dispatch

In mptcp_incoming_options() only the option parser was bracketed; the
dispatch that follows it for non-DSS options -- FASTCLOSE, ADD_ADDR with
its HMAC check, RM_ADDR, MP_PRIO, MP_FAIL and MP_RST handling -- ran
outside any section in the receive softirq. The PM handlers it calls
(mptcp_pm_add_addr_received(), mptcp_pm_add_addr_echoed(),
mptcp_pm_rm_addr_received(), mptcp_pm_mp_prio_received(),
mptcp_pm_mp_fail_received()) were therefore visible only when the
segment happened to be drained from the socket backlog in task context,
and a coverage-guided fuzzer read 0 PCs for RM_ADDR and MP_PRIO
handling even though those options are sent and acted on.

Open a section over the dispatch block, keyed on the same msk as the
parser section. It is a section of its own rather than an extension of
the parser one so that the common DSS-only packet pays nothing extra:
the block is only entered for a non-DSS suboption set. It closes before
the DSS/ACK processing below, which reaches the deferred-push section
through ack_update_msk() -> __mptcp_check_push(); the two never overlap.
There is no early exit inside the block, so a single start/stop pair is
balanced.

The inner add_addr_hmac_valid() bracket is dropped: it sits inside the
new section and would nest (kcov warns "started twice"); the wider
section records the same site, under the same key.

Nesting check: the block reaches PM bookkeeping, mptcp_pm_schedule_work()
and netlink events (mptcp_event*()), tcp_send_ack() on MP_FAIL (transmit
hands the segment to netif_rx(), deferred) and the FASTCLOSE work
scheduling; none opens a section. The fallback early-return path at the
top of the function, which calls __mptcp_check_push() directly, is
outside the new section. The same code running in task context from the
backlog drain stays on per-task kcov through the in_serving_softirq()
guard.

Instrumentation-only, no functional change; no-op under CONFIG_KCOV=n.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PnC9KL4QuZ7vdAomuT6sTC
---
 net/mptcp/options.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/mptcp/options.c b/net/mptcp/options.c
index 103a71e646b6..ab51bb1a7ee1 100644
--- a/net/mptcp/options.c
+++ b/net/mptcp/options.c
@@ -1182,12 +1182,10 @@ static bool add_addr_hmac_valid(struct mptcp_sock *msk,
 				struct mptcp_options_received *mp_opt)
 {
 	u64 hmac = 0;
-	bool valid;
 
 	if (mp_opt->echo)
 		return true;
 
-	mptcp_kcov_remote_start(msk);
 	hmac = add_addr_generate_hmac(READ_ONCE(msk->remote_key),
 				      READ_ONCE(msk->local_key),
 				      &mp_opt->addr);
@@ -1195,9 +1193,7 @@ static bool add_addr_hmac_valid(struct mptcp_sock *msk,
 	pr_debug("msk=%p, ahmac=%llu, mp_opt->ahmac=%llu\n",
 		 msk, hmac, mp_opt->ahmac);
 
-	valid = hmac == mp_opt->ahmac;
-	mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(msk);
-	return valid;
+	return hmac == mp_opt->ahmac;
 }
 
 static bool mptcp_over_limit(struct sock *sk, struct sock *ssk,
@@ -1267,6 +1263,14 @@ bool mptcp_incoming_options(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 		return sk->sk_state != TCP_CLOSE;
 
 	if (unlikely(mp_opt.suboptions != OPTION_MPTCP_DSS)) {
+		/* The non-DSS option dispatch (FASTCLOSE, ADD_ADDR and its
+		 * HMAC check, RM_ADDR, MP_PRIO, MP_FAIL, MP_RST) runs here in
+		 * the receive softirq; attribute it like the parser above.  A
+		 * section of its own, closed before the DSS/ACK processing
+		 * below, which reaches the deferred-push section through
+		 * ack_update_msk().  No early exit inside the block.
+		 */
+		mptcp_kcov_remote_start(msk);
 		if ((mp_opt.suboptions & OPTION_MPTCP_FASTCLOSE) &&
 		    READ_ONCE(msk->local_key) == mp_opt.fc_recv_key) {
 			WRITE_ONCE(msk->rcv_fastclose, true);
@@ -1307,6 +1311,7 @@ bool mptcp_incoming_options(struct sock *sk, struct sk_buff *skb)
 			subflow->reset_transient = mp_opt.reset_transient;
 			MPTCP_INC_STATS(sock_net(sk), MPTCP_MIB_MPRSTRX);
 		}
+		mptcp_kcov_remote_stop(msk);
 
 		if (!(mp_opt.suboptions & OPTION_MPTCP_DSS))
 			return true;
